// Lifting must keep a dependency on two reads that the arms test jointly,
// under sMRD.
//
// Thread 1 writes z := 1 exactly when r1 = 1 and r2 = 1 agree: on the
// then-arm under r2 = 1 && r1 = 1, on the else-arm under r2 != 1 && r1 != 1.
// Thread 2 copies z into x and y. The outcome r1 = r2 = r3 = 1 is thin air:
// the write of z would justify the reads it depends on.
//
// sMRD's Lifting gives the two writes the disjunction of their predicates,
// (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1) || (r1 != 1 && r2 != 1), which still depends on both
// reads. MoRDor lifted them to the conjuncts the arms share, here none, so
// the write depended on nothing and the outcome was admitted: 101 executions,
// Contradicted (#203). It now lifts only predicates that differ in a single
// complementary conjunct. LIFT-TWO-CONJUNCTS-SWAPPED.lit nests the tests the
// other way round, and was forbidden throughout: the conjuncts arrived in an
// order the old test refused.
x := 0; y := 0; z := 0;
{
  r1 := x;
  r2 := y;
  if (r2 = 1) {
    if (r1 = 1) {
      z := 1
    }
  } else {
    if (r1 != 1) {
      z := 1
    }
  }
} ||| {
  r3 := z;
  x := r3;
  y := r3
}
%%
forbid (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 1) [sMRD]
